Package: visualbrief
Title: Turn Campaign Data into Clear, Reusable Visual Reports
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Pablo", "Sánchez-Núñez", email = "psancheznunez@outlook.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-7845-9506"))
Description: Standardises the results of digital marketing and communication
    campaigns exported from advertising platforms, social media tools, web
    analytics or spreadsheets, and turns them into summaries, comparisons of
    content across audiences with confidence intervals, branded charts and a
    self-contained HTML report. Rates use Wilson score intervals and
    differences use Newcombe's hybrid score intervals (Newcombe, 1998,
    <doi:10.1002/(SICI)1097-0258(19980430)17:8%3C873::AID-SIM779%3E3.0.CO;2-I>).
    Brand colours can be read from a 'brand.yml' file and checked against the
    contrast requirements of the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines.
    Results are presented as descriptions of what happened in a campaign, not
    as causal claims about what makes content work.
